current_production_conversation_synthesis: TinyRustLM.com is deployed as a local-or-companion browser chat surface and no project-domain `.slm` route serves model bytes. Its secure loopback companion uses exact loopback/Host/Origin/CORS checks, one-time pairing, volatile origin-bound capabilities, replay-resistant mutations, receipt-bound model streaming, and no persisted credentials. MiniModel.org publishes two truthful metadata rows and reports zero active models and zero peers until current outside-network proof exists. Active conversation mode hides starter/setup surfaces and renders each assistant response once. Local package and symbol pairs are version 0.1.10; win-x64, linux-x64, and linux-arm64 releases execute with ABI v2. Deployment, 44/44 public asset hashes, five 404 boundaries, 28/28 Playwright cases, 56 Tiny JavaScript tests, 12 MiniModel JavaScript tests, and 166 .NET tests pass. NuGet.org publication, signing, outside proof, public announcement, and service installation remain unperformed. Authority: `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-web-companion-production-memory-2026-07-13.md`, SHA256 `ea8c1633e92e9b119840615ee25e0448f356c69f0d8c3def8172a262576bff3b`.
current_browser_prefix_cache_performance_synthesis: SUPERSEDED performance checkpoint. The checked portable runtime candidate reduced official repeated-turn latency from 61,890 ms to 10,678 ms by package-scoped release optimization, blockwise q4 accumulation, final-only prompt projection, and fail-closed exact-prefix KV reuse. Its 377,166-byte WASM required no SIMD; second-turn diagnostics proved 63 reused plus 19 computed tokens equaled the 82-token prompt. Strict visible/raw outputs were byte-identical, so the slice changed execution speed only. Its deployment-pending and 3/7 quality statements are historical; use `current_production_conversation_synthesis` for production routing. The original durable/machine hashes are `34028b8c0b057733a5ff7e75590e4f9a8caa945e1e4be0b52e013965f8e9769c` / `92b3002ba23fa9ae46b9bf24db6ae9da625d102d94a4060fb589fc049277d3ae`.
