current_multi_turn_conversation_context_2026_07_12: Normal chat retains at most six complete prior turns with model-aware formatting and passed real q4 browser recall. The strict one-call gate now separates evaluator integrity from output quality and rejects retries, repair, prefixes, field assembly, and answer injection. Current q4 is 3/7; SmolLM2 1.7B and Qwen2.5 1.5B peak at 4/7; Qwen3 1.7B, two prompt variants, reviewed examples, and the existing preservation-KL adapter do not improve that ceiling. No model is promoted. Shared failures are conflict confirmation, untrusted-memory precedence plus current-task continuation, and feasible resource-constrained fallback. Authority: `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-multi-turn-conversation-memory-2026-07-12.md`, SHA256 `9e8e8d909a1a073e4e5fca3667f2463eeffc8be806abdf8c2817fb3838f10c79`; comparison receipt SHA256 `686fb208640cf7787b6af77768310018a8a69d695bf204b2c8c7bf466955e28e`.
current_q5_footprint_fidelity_runtime_2026_07_12: `q5_0` is implemented and verified across `.slm` parsing/validation, native matvec and generation, sparse/low-rank adapters, public inspection, WASM diagnostics/corrupt-scale recovery, and protected NuGet packaging. `mixed-q5-matrix-f32-norm-v1` is 414,633,280 bytes versus 602,862,400 for q8-matrix/f32-norm, but reaches only 4/8 source argmax, minimum centered cosine 0.961345, and max JS 0.176864. Two larger mixed experiments also remained 4/8 and are rejected. Q5 is opt-in runtime evidence, not selector/default/browser/assistant admission. Authority: `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-q5-footprint-fidelity-memory-2026-07-12.md`, SHA256 `1cb4412dfeb5bf3ad1604efb2caba927804171464b8877291019f2fb7f3a160e`.
