current_no_cheat_json_trust_tier_slice_2026_07_08: `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-no-cheat-json-trust-tier-memory-2026-07-08.md` records the first implemented slice after the 2026-07-08 bleeding-edge intake. The locked TinyRustLM.com UI was preserved while JSON prompt-card output moved from the removed browser-side `generate_structured_json` helper into Rust/WASM `generate_status_reason_json`, which derives fields through runtime generation and serializes the final JSON in Rust. Browser trust metadata now labels models as `demo-fixture`, `experimental`, or `quality`; SmolLM2 q4 is quality-capable only when manifest, checksum, shape, prompt-format, runtime-smoke, eval, safety, and no-cheat evidence all pass, while q8 remains experimental and toy fixtures remain demo-only. Catalog rows claiming assistant quality fail closed unless they declare the full metadata-only `.slm` trust envelope and no project-server-byte admission. Rebuilt WASM manifest is `198002` bytes with checksum `0xd3b1120953a9ba13`. Verification passed across Rust runtime tests, slm-pack tests, .NET tests, WASM ABI smoke, prompt-card smoke, assistant-quality trust-tier smoke, source/Hugging Face discovery smoke, visual lock, formatting, syntax checks, and `git diff --check`.
current_bleeding_edge_system_plan_2026_07_08: `docs/report-intake/2026-07-08/tinyrustlm-bleeding-edge-intake-synthesis-2026-07-08.md`, `docs/report-intake/2026-07-08/tinyrustlm-bleeding-edge-tdd-plan-2026-07-08.md`, and `wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-bleeding-edge-system-plan-memory-2026-07-08.md` record the initial 31-report pass, now superseded for inventory purposes by `current_expanded_distillation_compression_intake_2026_07_08`. The durable strategy remains useful: preserve the approved TinyRustLM.com UI with visual locks, improve real `.slm` output only through Rust/WASM, keep fixture/demo evidence separate from assistant-quality claims, add strict `.slm` trust sidecars and policy tiers, use fixed plus seeded holdout honest eval, grow MiniModel/P2P through metadata-first verified `.slm` sharing, compress through compatible model selection/distillation/q8 reference/q6-g128/q5-g128/q4-a128-plus-outliers, and keep NuGet/open-core APIs narrow enough to protect private authoring, ranking, routing, optimizer, telemetry, licensing, and orchestration internals.
current_quality_ui_lock_synthesis_2026_07_07: The active TinyRustLM quality/UI-lock objective lives in `docs/report-intake/2026-07-07/tinyrustlm-quality-ui-lock-goal-2026-07-07.md`; it requires preserving the approved live UI exactly while making real `.slm` responses coherent through the same Rust/WASM path used by the browser. Current implementation adds screenshot/signature UI locks, no-cheat six-fixed-plus-six-seeded-holdout honest eval, manifest-backed prompt/capability metadata, prompt-format routing in browser/eval paths, sidecar normalization (`none`, `not-applicable`, `empty-output`), and quality-evidence validation that does not accept exact canned-answer matching. The assistant-quality gate now requires `honest-assistant-quality-v1`, `no_cheat_status=pass`, zero no-cheat failures, positive fixed and holdout counts, a numeric holdout seed, per-case `origin=fixed|holdout`, and non-fixture/non-plumbing quality claims; fixture-exact eval sidecars fail closed before converted-trained browser selector admission. The 2026-07-08 `stories15m-bpe` route now plans, reviews, converts, validates, and runs the real Xenova Stories-15M safetensors checkpoint with tied `lm_head.weight` alias handling and `llama-bpe-v1`/`LBPE` tokenizer preservation; the resulting q8 `.slm` produces real local runtime text but fails honest assistant quality 0/12 because it is a raw Stories completion model, not an instruction/chat assistant. The 2026-07-08 SmolLM2 route now includes grouped-query runtime support, `gpt2-bpe-v1`/`GBPE` tokenizer/source planning, and a served quality-capable `tinyrustlm/models/smollm2-360m-instruct-q4.slm` artifact from `HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-360M-Instruct`: q4_0, 227667520 bytes, `.slm` checksum `0x8b5aa7ec4abeed93`, eval case-evidence checksum `0xf63dee70df605f05`, native release eval 12/12 fixed plus seeded holdout cases, `quality-gate assistant-quality` pass, locked browser assistant-quality smoke pass with selected `smollm2q4`, and prompt-card browser smoke pass through visible Summarize/Code/Rewrite/JSON cards using the same q4 Rust/WASM path. The prompt-card smoke records code `This code adds two integers together.` and structured JSON `{"status":"local","reason":"In browser local runtime model where prompts stay"}` while still noting summarize wording roughness. Runtime `.slm` fail-closed validation now rejects malformed-but-checksummed tensor metadata, non-finite f32 payloads, and non-positive/non-finite q8/q4 scales in the shared Rust/WASM load path; the rebuilt served WASM manifest is `187243` bytes with checksum `0xfd09af080dd804f0`, and `wasm-abi-smoke` proves `malformedSlmPayload=passed` by corrupting a q8 scale, refreshing the `.slm` checksum, receiving `invalid header`, reloading the valid model, and continuing generation/adapter/free-model checks. Browser `model-malformed` smoke now proves the locked UI also rejects a corrupt-but-checksummed q8 `.slm` with `Model rejected`, `error 6`, `invalid header`, `model_loaded=false`, disabled generate/reset/step controls, enabled selector recovery, and no remote-origin requests. The UI verifier now has `-RunVisualLock`, and the Bash verifier has `RUN_VISUAL_LOCK=1`, comparing approved desktop/mobile shell fields against the live baseline with screenshot evidence; current visual proof passed with `baseline_failures=[]` and reports under `artifacts/reports/ui-lock-verification/`. Broader product completion remains open for output polish across more unseen prompts, performance, deployment/live proof, and no-private-internals boundaries.
